# The assessment of MODEL-ROUTE-016 against this build. The requirement identifier is
# this file's stem and appears nowhere inside it, because a second place to spell the
# identity is a second place for it to be wrong -- the rule OD-SPEC-007 chose for a
# record registration, and CHK-003.assessment states for this registry.
#
# MODEL-ROUTE-016: "Context assembly shall be separately observable and attributable.
# Retrieval, filtering, authority resolution, deduplication, compression, prompt or
# task-envelope projection, request construction, model inference, and post-response
# validation shall emit separate causally linked TelemetryJunctions with resource,
# latency, cache, usage, and evidence status where available."
#
# PipelineStage and TelemetryJunction carry the nine named stages and five named
# observability fields, plus a caused_by link making a chain of junctions causally linked.
# Nothing emits one, and P40-MODEL-ROUTING-DISPATCH-WIRING did not change that: it decided
# which backend answers a task, not how a task is assembled.
#
# The gap moves anyway, because the old one cited a site that now has real consumers. One
# of the nine stages does exist in this workspace, which is what makes the rest measurable:
# Bare_Task is task-envelope projection -- it builds a TaskEnvelope from a goal and an
# effort, and emits no junction, records no resource or latency, and has nothing to be
# caused_by. The other eight stages have no implementation at all. There is no retrieval,
# no filtering, no authority resolution, no deduplication, no compression, no separate
# request-construction step, and no post-response validation; a dispatch hands the envelope
# to a backend and reads what comes back.
verdict: Partial
site: crates/packages/nomos-model-package/src/telemetry_junction.rs#TelemetryJunction
gap: crates/orchestration/nomos-agent-orchestration/src/run.rs#Bare_Task
